  "id": "channel",
  "term": "channel",
  "definition": "In this context, a channel is a protein pathway in a cell membrane that allows specific ions such as calcium or sodium to move into the neuron when the membrane’s electrical state changes or when certain stimuli activate it. This ion flow helps start nerve depolarization or trigger neurotransmitter release, allowing signals such as pain information to be passed along neurons.",
